#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175746 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/id #uuid "ef520918-4e4b-516b-acaa-57a14b5c1405" :question/math-academy-id "e-16134" :question/problem "Calculate $\\textrm{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx = \\big\\{ 6, \\: -2, \\: 7, \\: 1 \\big\\},\\qquad\ny = \\big\\{ 5, \\: -1, \\: 4, \\: 0 \\big\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\big\\{ x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}$ and $y=\\big\\{ y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) =  \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$ and $\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n y_i$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (6+(-2)+7+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (5+(-1)+4+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-3)(5-2)+(-2-3)(-1-2)+(7-3)(4-2)+(1-3)(0-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(3)(3)+(-5)(-3)+(4)(2)+(-2)(-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[9+15+8+4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 36 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175747 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/id #uuid "33adfe2b-297e-5c52-8c4f-088d0c2b66e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-16136" :question/problem "| **Number of Hours of Sleep ($x$)** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Points Scored ($y$)** | $54$ | $68$ | $80$ | $90$ |\n\nA math teacher asked four of her students how many hours they had slept the night before an exam. The information she received is shown in the table above. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overline{x}=5$ and $\\overline{y}=73.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\big\\{ x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}$ and $y=\\big\\{ y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) =  \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$ and $\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n y_i$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2-5)(54-73)+(4-5)(68-73)+(6-5)(80-73)+(8-5)(90-73)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-3)(-19)+(-1)(-5)+(1)(7)+(3)(17)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[57+5+7+51] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 120 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2cf924-a64f-54dc-87a7-a55cc5608322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266557} {:answer/id #uuid "8a368b61-2a10-5572-b96f-d946e6484613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267374} {:answer/id #uuid "9890bce2-eb7b-5966-b1f6-aba325b542fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267516} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c4e622-7bf6-58a1-a061-53fb05257cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267655} {:answer/id #uuid "ea073cde-0957-5f5a-929b-80323be6c7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea073cde-0957-5f5a-929b-80323be6c7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268231} :answer-field/id #uuid "18f8d6d5-cdcc-531f-802a-b52a41c57580" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b3a2205-203a-5056-a951-45e86cc0afea" :question/math-academy-id "q-134066" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={4,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,5},\\,y={6,\\,3,\\,12,\\,11}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=2$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=8.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-2)(6-8)+(-1-2)(3-8)+(0-2)(12-8)+(5-2)(11-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2)(-2)+(-3)(-5)+(-2)(4)+(3)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[-4+15-8+9] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9087cd44-503a-51c3-8f04-40fe65b14ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174269} {:answer/id #uuid "caaf81a9-a943-54a0-870a-d117dd946a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174270} {:answer/id #uuid "f621b923-d136-5bb2-93dd-bd0a11dcee65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174271} {:answer/id #uuid "00bb18e0-d159-5339-a1de-8278df118689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174272} {:answer/id #uuid "66cff592-58f2-5a82-be01-0cf2cda0a8b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174273}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9ddb89-9b77-521c-b63e-2dd998d851d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174268}] :question/id #uuid "41c31e68-b6d7-5283-bb82-6cc7ac671a08" :question/math-academy-id "q-134079" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $6$ | $10$ | $12$ | $16$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Education, in years ($y$)** | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n\nThe table above shows the ages and corresponding years of formal education completed by each of Mark's cousins.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given th